{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I sell the morning paper, sir
My name is Jimmy [D]Brown,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Everybody knows I am,
The Newsboy of the [G]town.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]You will hear me yelling "Morning Star",
As I run along the [D]street,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I have no hat up on my head,
No shoes upon my [G]feet.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]I have no hat up on my head,
No [C]shoes upon my [G]feet
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[G]I'm awful cold and hungry, sir,
My clothes are worn and [D]thin,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
I wander 'bout from place to place,
My daily bread to [G]win.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[G]Never mind, sir, how I look,
Don't look at me and [D]frown,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 9}
I sell the morning papers, sir,
My name is Jimmy [G]Brown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 10}
[G]I sell the morning papers, sir,
My [C]name is Jimmy [G]Brown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 11}
[G]My Father died a drunkard, sir,
I've heard my Mother [D]say,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 12}
And I am helping Mother, sir,
As I journey on my [G]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 13}
[G]Mother always tells me, sir,
I've nothing in this world to [D]lose,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 14}
I'll get a place in Heaven, sir,
To sell the Gospel [G]News.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 15}
[G]Never mind sir how I look,
Don't look at me and [D]frown,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 16}
I sell the morning papers, sir,
My name is Jimmy [G]Brown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 17}
[G]I sell the morning papers, sir,
My [C]name is Jimmy [G]Brown
